/*
# Tooltip

The layer system's floor: any view sets `tooltipLabel = "…"` and this singleton renders
it — hover delay, placement, flip, and theming are nobody's problem at the use
site. It arrives automatically when any view in the program carries a tip, as
`FocusRing` does; declare your own `Tooltip [ ]` (or subclass) to replace the
rendition.

It listens to the Tooltips service (a `Tooltips [ onTooltip(e: TooltipEvent) { … } ]` member), which owns the platform
conventions (the show delay — `tooltipDelay`, ~1s in the Cupertino and Redmond
conventions, ~500ms MountainView — instant retarget while showing, hide on
press). **Placement is theme data too** (`tooltipPlacement`): "below" (the
default — under the target, centered, flipping above at the edge), "above"
(flipping below), or "pointer" (the Cupertino help tag —
offset below-right of where the cursor rests). Always clamped inside the
app. Pure chrome — never focusable, never a pointer target, always above
content (the auto-splice puts it last in the App, and source order stacks).

Theming (the four cities carry the tokens): `tooltipFill` / `tooltipTextColor` /
`tooltipStrokeColor` (null = no border) / `tooltipFontSize` (11 in Cupertino, 12
elsewhere). Cupertino and Redmond wear bordered surface chips; San
Francisco and Mountain View the inverse chip.

**You do not instantiate this.** Set `tooltipLabel` on any view and the singleton appears; the
members below exist for a subclass that replaces the rendition.

```declare
View [ x = 20, y = 20, width = 130, height = 38, cornerRadius = 8, fill = steelblue,
    tooltipLabel = "Saves your changes",
    Text [ x = center, y = center, textColor = white, text = "Save" ]
    ]
```

## label
The text currently displayed, pushed in by the `Tooltips` service from the hovered view's
`tooltipLabel`. **A subclass reads this; nothing writes it from app code.**

## placement
Where the chip sits, elected by `provided("theme").tooltipPlacement`: `"below"` (the default,
centred under the target, flipping above at the edge), `"above"` (the Fluent default,
flipping below), or `"pointer"` (the Cupertino help tag, offset below-right of the resting
cursor). Always clamped inside the app.

## ex
**Internal.** The target's root-space x, for placement.

## ey
**Internal.** The target's root-space y.

## ew
**Internal.** The target's width.

## eh
**Internal.** The target's height.

## px
**Internal.** The pointer's x where it came to rest, for `"pointer"` placement.

## py
**Internal.** The pointer's y where it came to rest.

## visible
Shown only when asked and there is text to show — an empty tip never paints a bare box.

## width
Sized to its text plus padding, so the box fits the words and never the other way round.

## height
Sized to its text plus padding, one line or several.

## x
Beside the pointer, or centred under the element, then clamped inside the app with a 4px margin — a tip near an edge slides in rather than clipping.

## y
Below the pointer, or below or above the element as `placement` says, flipping to the other side when the preferred one would leave the app.

## fill
The theme's tooltip ground when it names one, else a dark slate — a tip is the one surface that stays dark on a light theme.

## stroke
A hairline only when the theme names a tooltip line; flat themes get none.

## selectable
Chrome, never prose: a tip's text does not select, even inside a `selectable` region — the same provision every `Control` makes for its label.

## cornerRadius
From the theme's `tooltipCornerRadius` (4 by default).
*/

include [ "floating.declare" ]

class Tooltip extends Floating [
    // a Floating in the floating layer (floating.declare): above everything in
    // the app, taking no focus and no keys; presses pass through it, and a
    // scroll aimed past it puts it away. It appears and goes at once.

    kind = "floating",
    pressPolicy = "ignore",
    scrollPolicy = "dismiss",
    visible = { shown && label != "" },

    label: string = "",
    ex: number = 0,                              // the target's root-space box
    ey: number = 0,
    ew: number = 0,
    eh: number = 0,
    px: number = 0,                              // the pointer at show (the "pointer" placement)
    py: number = 0,

    tips: Tooltips [
        onTooltip(e: TooltipEvent) {
            if (e == null || e.root != app) { classroot.close(); return }
            classroot.ex = e.x; classroot.ey = e.y; classroot.ew = e.w; classroot.eh = e.h
            classroot.px = app.pointerX; classroot.py = app.pointerY   // the pointer as it rests at show
            classroot.label = e.text
            classroot.show()
            }
        ],

    // geometry derives from the label's measured size; placement is a theme
    // election (below | above | pointer), always flipped when it would leave
    // the app and clamped horizontally

    placement: string = { provided("theme").tooltipPlacement },

    width  = { this.t.width + 16 },
    height = { this.t.height + 10 },
    x = { Math.max(4, Math.min(app.width - this.width - 4,
            placement == "pointer" ? px + 10 : ex + (ew - this.width) / 2)) },
    y = { placement == "pointer"
            ? (py + 18 + this.height > app.height ? py - this.height - 8 : py + 18)
            : placement == "above"
                ? (ey - this.height - 7 < 0 ? ey + eh + 7 : ey - this.height - 7)
                : (ey + eh + 7 + this.height > app.height ? ey - this.height - 7 : ey + eh + 7) },

    cornerRadius = { provided("theme").tooltipCornerRadius },
    fill   = { provided("theme").tooltipFill },
    stroke = { provided("theme").tooltipStrokeColor != null ? stroke(1, provided("theme").tooltipStrokeColor) : null },

    // pure chrome: never a pointer target — and never on the hover chain
    // either, which is what pointerEvents (unlike a hit-test override) governs.
    // "none" applies to this view only, not its children (View.pointerEvents), so
    // the label must carry it too, or it would answer viewAt and sit on the hover chain.

    pointerEvents = "none",

    // chrome, not prose: a tip never selects inside a `selectable` region

    selectable = false,

    t: Text [ pointerEvents = "none",
        x = 8, y = 5, fontSize = { provided("theme").tooltipFontSize },
        textColor = { provided("theme").tooltipTextColor },
        text = { classroot.label } ]
    ]
